1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,904
Part one. The debut.

2
00:00:02,392 --> 00:00:04,795
How did the year's biggest AI listing go?

3
00:00:05,224 --> 00:00:07,477
Anthropic, the maker of Claude,

4
00:00:07,744 --> 00:00:09,985
listed at $83 a share.

5
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:11,738
As Zitron recorded,

6
00:00:11,784 --> 00:00:12,934
it traded higher,

7
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:15,348
but struggled to stay above $100.

8
00:00:15,708 --> 00:00:19,110
His verdict: not the massive return people expected.

9
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,409
But first days say little.

10
00:00:21,838 --> 00:00:23,510
So let's look at the business.

11
00:00:23,777 --> 00:00:24,973
First, growth.

12
00:00:25,751 --> 00:00:27,713
Citing spending data from Ramp,

13
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:30,674
he says Anthropic's growth this quarter is trending

14
00:00:30,743 --> 00:00:32,856
toward 15 to 25%.

15
00:00:33,286 --> 00:00:34,238
A quarter ago,

16
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:35,875
it was 47%.

17
00:00:36,142 --> 00:00:37,628
A few quarters before that,

18
00:00:37,675 --> 00:00:39,312
around 150%.

19
00:00:39,730 --> 00:00:41,471
That's not a rocket anymore.

20
00:00:41,738 --> 00:00:43,654
That's a rocket running out of fuel.

21
00:00:44,409 --> 00:00:45,059
Now the bills.

22
00:00:45,094 --> 00:00:49,378
Anthropic has signed up for $895 billion of

23
00:00:49,459 --> 00:00:53,267
commitments, mostly computing power that hasn't even started.

24
00:00:53,615 --> 00:00:55,926
And $435 billion

25
00:00:56,286 --> 00:00:57,528
of that, he says,

26
00:00:57,609 --> 00:00:58,735
can't be cancelled.

27
00:00:59,223 --> 00:01:00,825
Here's the number that really matters.

28
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:04,993
The Financial Times' Robert Armstrong calculated that for

29
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:06,270
a decent return,

30
00:01:06,503 --> 00:01:09,359
Anthropic would need about $600 billion of revenue

31
00:01:09,382 --> 00:01:10,821
a year by 2030.

32
00:01:11,599 --> 00:01:15,117
Microsoft, with monopolies across office software,

33
00:01:15,465 --> 00:01:18,588
made about $331 billion last year.

34
00:01:18,925 --> 00:01:21,224
Anthropic would need nearly twice that.

35
00:01:21,561 --> 00:01:22,350
To be fair,

36
00:01:22,478 --> 00:01:23,418
there's a cushion:

37
00:01:23,836 --> 00:01:27,064
over $200 billion in cash after the IPO,

38
00:01:27,365 --> 00:01:28,480
by Zitron's count.

39
00:01:29,014 --> 00:01:30,871
But big prepayments are coming,

40
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:34,401
and he says anything under $21 billion of

41
00:01:34,482 --> 00:01:36,305
revenue this quarter would be a problem.

42
00:01:36,792 --> 00:01:38,464
Even 15% growth,

43
00:01:38,487 --> 00:01:39,405
in his math,

44
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:40,391
isn't enough.

45
00:01:40,821 --> 00:01:42,562
Which raises the obvious question.

46
00:01:43,050 --> 00:01:44,397
Who was buying these shares,

47
00:01:44,432 --> 00:01:45,419
and why?
